<body>
    <h1>Environment Setup</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>ISOs are on &nbsp;\\dsstbsoftware\Software\</strong></p>
<p><br></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col>
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>OS Setup for <span style=3D"color: rgb(2=
55,0,0);">AWS Workspaces</span>:</strong></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><p><strong><br>First take note tha=
t AWS Workspaces are expensive to run and will therefor hibernate automatic=
ally after 1hr of inactivity.<br><br></strong>1) Download and install the a=
ppropriate AWS Workspaces client on your personal PC or laptop here :&nbsp;=
<a href=3D"https://clients.amazonworkspaces.com/" class=3D"external-link" r=
el=3D"nofollow">https://clients.amazonworkspaces.com/</a><br>2) Register th=
e workspace using the registration code you received via email or Teams.<br=
>3) Login using your username without the domain. So instead of MIX\BobM, j=
ust uses BobM. The password is your MIX domain password provided via email =
or Teams.<br>4) When using an AWS Workspace, you do not need to install any=
 VPN software to connect to the MiX network. You will automatically have ac=
cess to the Development and Integration environments (not UAT or production=
 though, that is on a different domain).<br>5)&nbsp;<span>Install Office. D=
o this by opening a browser window to <a href=3D"http://portal.office365.co=
m" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">portal.office365.com</a> and lo=
gin with your email address and domain account password. You can choose to =
install the Office desktop app by clicking on the "Install Office" dropdown=
 and following the options.<br>6) Open the Server Manager. Click on "Local =
Server" on the left. Turn IE Enhanced Security Configuration OFF for both U=
sers and Administrators (otherwise you will have trouble signing into Visua=
l Studio later).<br><strong>It is recommended to set up 2 factor authentica=
tion by installing the Microsoft Authenticator app on your phone.</strong><=
br></span></p><p><strong><span style=3D"color: rgb(64,64,64);">Add Windows =
Features:</span></strong></p><p><span>1) Go to Turn Windows Features On or =
Off (in Programs and Features). The Server Manager will open. Click next un=
til you get to Server Roles.<br>2) Check Web Server and add the IIS Managem=
ent Console.<br></span><span>3) If you are installing SQL 2014 specifically=
, check .NET Framework 3.5. Not required for SQL 2016 and up. Local SQL is =
not required for general full stack development. Generally only if you are =
in a reporting/data systems team.<br></span><span>4) Check </span><span>Mes=
sage Queuing.<br>5) Expand the Message Queuing tree view and check Director=
y Service Integration.<br>6) Click next to configure the Web Server Role Se=
rvices.<br>7) Expand Application Development and check&nbsp;.NET Extensibil=
ity 4.7 and click Add Features.<br>8) Check ASP.NET4.7 and click Add Featur=
es.<br>9) Check the WebSocket Protocol.<br>10) Click Next and Install.<br><=
/span>11) Skip the next section for standalone desktops and continue with "=
IIS Setup"</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col>
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong><span style=3D"color: rgb(64,64,64);">OS=
 Setup for <span style=3D"color: rgb(255,0,0);">Desktops</span>:</span></st=
rong></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"1" class=3D"confluenceTd"><p><span>1) If your desktop did no=
t come pre-installed with Windows, install the latest Enterprise flavour of=
 Windows.<br></span><span>2) At the first sign in screen, there is no need =
to sign in with a Microsoft account. Select create a new account and then "=
Sign in without a Microsoft account".&nbsp;</span><span>Don't bother enteri=
ng your real name as the user account, you will get a new one when you are =
added to the domain.<br></span><span>3) Depending on your version of Window=
s, disable the Windows Media Network Sharing Service (unless you want to sh=
are your music with everyone)<br></span><span>4) Unless you are already on =
the MiX domain and have a valid username and password, don't bother customi=
sing the OS, your PC must be added to the domain which means you will get a=
 new user profile.<br></span><span>5) If you are not on the MiX domain yet,=
 get MiX IT or Stephan Visagie to add you to the MIX domain.<br></span><spa=
n>6) Log in with your MIX credentials. Now you can customise your OS.<br></=
span><span>7) If you have a Dell, go to <a href=3D"http://support.dell.com"=
 class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">support.dell.com</a> and search f=
or your service tag (label on the PC/laptop). Download and install any driv=
ers you think you will need. In general,&nbsp;</span><span>download the Chi=
pset and graphics drivers.<br></span><span>8)&nbsp;Install Office. Do this =
by opening a browser window to <a href=3D"http://portal.office365.com" clas=
s=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">portal.office365.com</a> and login wit=
h your email address and domain account password. You can choose to install=
 the Office desktop app by clicking on the "Install Office" dropdown and fo=
llowing the options.<br><strong>It is recommended to set up 2 factor authen=
tication by installing the Microsoft Authenticator app on your phone.</stro=
ng></span><span><br></span></p><p><strong><span style=3D"color: rgb(64,64,6=
4);">Add Windows Features:</span></strong></p><p><span>In addition to what =
is already checked:<br>1) Go to Turn Windows Features On or Off (in Program=
s and Features).<br>2) If you are installing SQL 2014 specifically, check .=
NET Framework 3.5. Not required for SQL 2016 and up.&nbsp; Local SQL is not=
 required for general full stack development. Generally only if you are in =
a reporting/data systems team.<br></span><span>3) Check Internet Informatio=
n Services. Keep the default settings. Don't use IIS Express because VS mod=
ifies the project files.<br></span><span>4) Check IIS Management Console. U=
nder Application Development Features, check .NET Extensibility 4.7, ASP.NE=
T 4.7, ISAPI Extensions, ISAPI Filters.<br>5) Check IIS Management Console.=
 Under Common HTTP Features, check Static Content<br>6) Check </span><span>=
Microsoft Message Queue (MSMQ).<br>7) Expand the MSMQ tree view and check M=
SMQ Active Directory Domain Services integration.</span></p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p><strong style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;"><span style=3D"color: rgb(64,6=
4,64);"><br><br>IIS Setup:</span></strong></p>
<p><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">1) Once the features have been a=
dded, o</span><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">pen the IIS Manager.<=
br>2) Go to the DefaultAppPool properties and add development\srvciis accou=
nt details under "Identity". The password is "P4ssw0rd". You can also use y=
our own domain account, but you must then remember to change the App pool p=
assword every time you change your domain password - otherwise the App pool=
 will always be in a stopped state to prevent your account being locked.<br=
></span></p>
<p><br><strong>GIT Setup:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>&nbsp;Download and install the latest Git for Windows here :&nbsp;<a hr=
ef=3D"https://git-scm.com/download/win" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofo=
llow">https://git-scm.com/download/win</a>
<ol>
<li>NOTE: Make sure "Check out Windows, Commit Unix" line endings is checke=
d.</li>
<li>Keep the rest of the default settings checked (i.e. caching and git cre=
dential manager etc).</li>
</ol></li>
<li>OPTIONAL: Download and install a Git GUI interface if you don't want to=
 use the command line tools. Consider&nbsp;Tortoise Git :<a href=3D"https:/=
/tortoisegit.org/download/" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https:=
//tortoisegit.org/download/</a>&nbsp;or use SourceTree or Visual Studio's b=
uilt-in Git tools.<br>Whichever Git client you use, make sure your Name and=
 Email address is properly configured so that the commits you do are format=
ted correctly.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong><span style=3D"color: rgb(64,64,64);"><br>IDE Setup:<br></span><=
/strong></p>
<ol>
<li><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">You can decide to use Visual St=
udio Code if you want, depending on the team you are in and their requireme=
nts.<br><a href=3D"https://code.visualstudio.com/download" class=3D"externa=
l-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://code.visualstudio.com/download</a><br><br>=
For full framework development it is recommended to install Visual Studio. =
At the time of writing that is VS 2022.<br><a href=3D"https://visualstudio.=
microsoft.com/vs/professional" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">htt=
ps://visualstudio.microsoft.com/vs/professional</a><br>Choose "Enterprise" =
if you have an Enterprise level VS subscription. Most likely it will be Pro=
fessional.<br><br>Run the downloaded installer. Confirm that you are instal=
ling the correct version for your license. It should read "Installing - Vis=
ual Studio Professional"</span></li>
<li><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">For most common installations, =
choose <span> "ASP.NET and web development",&nbsp;</span>"Universal Windows=
 Platform development", ".NET desktop development", "Data storage and proce=
ssing"<br>Under "Individual Components" tab check all the .NET Framework <s=
trong>4.8</strong>&nbsp;items and also&nbsp;<span>".NET Portable Library ta=
rgeting pack" as well as TypeScript SDK</span><br>Under Data Storage And Pr=
ocessing, make sure SQL Server Data Tools is selected (SSDT).<br></span></l=
i>
<li><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Click Install and make coffee</=
span></li>
<li><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Set the VS shortcut to always s=
tart as Administrator, otherwise you will run into build issues <strong>OR =
(thanks to Ross for this), just browse to C:\Windows\System32\inetsrv\confi=
g and click on the button to confirm permissions.<br></strong></span><span =
style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">To achieve that, do this:</span>
<ol>
<li>Browse to devenv.exe (C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\2022\Pro=
fessional\Common7\IDE), right-click and select "Troubleshoot compatibility"=
. Select "Troubleshoot program"</li>
<li>Check "The program requires additional permissions"</li>
<li>Click "Next", click "Test the program..."</li>
<li>Wait for VS to launch.</li>
<li>If it is the first time you are running VS, click sign-in and enter you=
r email address (e.g. bob.morgan@mixtelematics.com) and your domain passwor=
d.</li>
<li>Close VS and click "Next"</li>
<li>Select "Yes, save these settings for this program"</li>
<li>Click "Close"</li>
</ol></li>
<li>Once VS is open, look for any updates by clicking on the yellow flag to=
p right.</li>
<li>Set tab spaces:
<ol>
<li>Tools &gt; Options &gt; Text Editor &gt; All Languages &gt; Tabs</li>
<li>Select Smart indenting. Set Tab size to 2, indenting to 2, and KEEP tab=
s.</li>
<li>Tools &gt; Options &gt; Text Editor &gt; T-SQL90 &gt; Tabs</li>
<li>Select Block indenting. Set Tab size to 2, indenting to 2, and INSERT S=
PACES.</li>
</ol></li>
<li>Install Redis x64 (<a href=3D"https://github.com/MSOpenTech/redis/relea=
ses/" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://github.com/MSOpenTec=
h/redis/releases/</a>) &lt;&lt;&lt; <strong>This should not be needed anymo=
re even for local development. Install only if you really need this</strong=
></li>
<li>Setup NuGet.
<ol>
<li>Open Visual Studio under TOOLS &gt; NuGet Package Manager &gt; Package =
Manager Settings set NuGet to automatically download packages.</li>
<li>Under "Package Sources", add the MiX NuGet package source: Name: MiX Az=
ure Path:&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/MiXTelematics/Common/_=
packaging/Common/nuget/v3/index.json" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofoll=
ow">https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/MiXTelematics/Common/_packaging/Common/nuget=
/v3/index.json</a></li>
</ol></li>
<li>Install AjaxMinifier. It is used by the Angular UI build process. (<a h=
ref=3D"https://github.com/microsoft/ajaxmin/releases/download/v5.14/Microso=
ft.Ajax.Minifier.v5.14.zip" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https:=
//github.com/microsoft/ajaxmin/releases/download/v5.14/Microsoft.Ajax.Minif=
ier.v5.14.zip</a>), otherwise you won't be able to build the UI Framework. =
Extract and run AjaxMinSetup.</li>
<li><p>Install PostSharp:</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Previously PostSharp was installed automatically when you build the =
DynaMiX.Backend project via NuGet. This does not seem to be the case with V=
S 2015+.</p></li>
<li>Download the PostSharp EXE here, <strong>THIS SPECIFIC VERSION</strong>=
 (4.3.48): <a href=3D"https://www.postsharp.net/downloads/postsharp-4.3/v4.=
3.38" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.postsharp.net/do=
wnloads/postsharp-4.3/v4.3.48</a></li>
<li>Don't select the trial or pro license, select <strong>PostSharp Express=
</strong>. When asked if you don't want to try PostSharp Ultimate, select <=
strong>No, thanks.</strong></li>
</ol></li>
<li>Install the Powershell Tools for Visual Studio extension to support the=
 automated deployment project types. Do this by going to the Extensions men=
u option and searching online for "powershell tools for VS 2022".</li>
<li>If you will be building the DynaMiX Backend, you <strong>MUST</strong> =
install the 2012 Visual C++ Redistributable Update 4 (64 bit version) - dow=
nloadable here:&nbsp;<a rel=3D"nofollow" href=3D"http://www.microsoft.com/e=
n-us/download/details.aspx?id=3D30679" class=3D"external-link">http://www.m=
icrosoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=3D30679</a>&nbsp;(<span style=
=3D"color: rgb(255,0,0);">it HAS to be this version, not something newer or=
 older</span>)</li>
<li>Download and install the TypeScript 3.8 SDK :&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://m=
arketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=3DTypeScriptTeam.typescript-38rc=
" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://marketplace.visualstudio=
.com/items?itemName=3DTypeScriptTeam.typescript-38rc</a></li>
<li>BUILD ORDER (Clone these projects in D:\Projects or C:\Projects):
<ol>
<li>Clone the DynaMiX.UI.Framework GIT repo, switch to the master branch, o=
pen in Visual Studio and build.</li>
<li>Clone the MiXFleet GIT repo, switch to the Integration branch, open in =
Visual Studio and build.</li>
<li>Clone the DynaMiX.Backend GIT repo, switch to the Integration branch, o=
pen in Visual Studio and build.</li>
</ol></li>
<li>OPTIONAL:
<ol>
<li>ReSharper (<a style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;" href=3D"https://www.jet=
brains.com/resharper/download/" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">ht=
tps://www.jetbrains.com/resharper/download/</a>) (get a key from Russell Si=
mmonds)</li>
<li>For those that had a perpetual key for ReSharper 8, you can install the=
 first version of ReSharper 9 only (9.0.0.0), filename:&nbsp;ReSharperAndTo=
olsPacked01Update1_checked.exe</li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong><span style=3D"color: rgb(64,64,64);">ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:<br>=
</span></strong><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">1) Add MSBUILD to y=
our path. Open Advanced System Settings and edit the PATH variable. Add ;C:=
\Windows\Microsoft.NET\Framework64\v4.0.30319\<br></span><span style=3D"lin=
e-height: 1.4285715;">2) If you have Visual Studio 2010 installed as well, =
add the following environment variable: "VisualStudioVersion" with value "1=
1.0"</span></p>
<p><strong><br></strong></p>
<p><strong>CLONE REPOSITORIES:<br></strong>The repositories to clone depend=
s which team you are in. Your Team Lead should provide you with the reposit=
ories you need to clone.<br>1) You can clone from within VS by clicking on =
Azure DevOps and signing in. Or if you prefer TortoiseGit or SourceTree, cl=
one repositories using that instead.<br>2) Clone the repository into C:\Pro=
jects\ (so you end up with C:\Projects\MiXFleet or C:\Projects\DynaMiX.Back=
end for example).<br>3) If you are prompted for a username and password, en=
ter your MiX email address and domain password.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong>NODEJS (for UI unit tests) - THIS WILL CHANGE SOON BECAUSE OF AN=
GULAR 4:</strong><br>1) Download and install NodeJS 64bit msi from <a href=
=3D"https://nodejs.org/download/" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">=
https://nodejs.org/download/</a><br>2) Install Karma. Open a command prompt=
 and navigate to C:\Program Files\nodejs\<br>3)&nbsp;npm install -g karma@0=
.12.31 -msvs_version=3D2015 &nbsp;(-msvs_version=3D2015 is only required if=
 you only have VS2015 installed)<br>4)&nbsp;npm install -g karma-jasmine@0.=
1.5 karma-cli@0.0.4 karma-chrome-launcher@0.1.7&nbsp;karma-sourcemap-loader=
</p>
<p>The versions above has to be used. Using a version above 0.1.5 of karma-=
jasmine will result in all unit tests failing due to version incompatibilit=
ies between jasmine and Angular 1.0.6/8 which we are using.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong>Local SQL Setup &lt;&lt;&lt;&lt; Just do steps 2 and 13. The ful=
l SQL installation is not needed anymore for general development:<br></stro=
ng><s><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">1) Install SQL Server 2016 De=
veloper Edition<br></span></s></p>
<ul style=3D"list-style-type: square;">
<li><s><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Choose New SQL Server stand-=
alone installation</span></s></li>
<li><s><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Select Database Engine Servi=
ces</span></s></li>
<li><s><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">In SQL 2016 SQL management s=
tudio is no longer available and you have to install SQL Management Tools s=
eparately (SMSS-Setup-ENU.exe).</span></s></li>
<li><s><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Check Windows AND SQL authen=
tication modes (Mixed Mode authentication). Enter an "sa" password. Under S=
pecify SQL administrators,&nbsp;</span></s></li>
<li><s><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Click "Add Current User" to =
add your domain account.</span></s></li>
<li><s><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">If you like, click on the "D=
ata Directories" tab and change the location of where the databases are cre=
ated, i.e. D:\MSSQLDbs\</span></s></li>
</ul>
<p>2) After installation, in Windows Services, set Distributed Transaction =
Coordinator to start automatically (delayed)<br><s>3) Open SQL Management S=
tudio. Connect to db (local). Right-click local DB, select properties. Clic=
k Memory tab and make max mem usage 1024MB.</s><br><s>4) Expand "Security &=
gt; Logins" and make sure your your domain user account is listed and that =
it has sysadmin rights.</s><br><s>5) If you used DEVELOPMENT\SRVCIIS for th=
e IIS DefaultAppPool login, add the DEVELOPMENT\SRVCIIS account as well and=
 assign sysadmin rights.</s><br><s>6) Get the DB backups and scripts (from =
\\dsstbisql01\Backups\DynaMiX\). If you don't have access, please ask Steph=
an Visagie.</s><br><s>7) Edit the "Restore all.sql" file and change the Sql=
Backup path (where the .bak files are) and the target Data and Log path (wh=
ere you want your databases to be restored to - your SQL data path).</s><br=
><s><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">8) Open SQL management studio o=
pen the "Restore all.sql" script.<br>9) Enter SQLCMD mode. Query -&gt; SQLC=
MD Mode<br>10) Execute the restore script.<br></span></s><span style=3D"lin=
e-height: 1.4285715;"><s>11) Open and execute Logins.sql.</s><br><s>12) Ope=
n and execute Set CLR Enabled.sql.</s><br></span><span style=3D"line-height=
: 1.4285715;">13) Setup MSDTC in Component services<br></span></p>
<ul style=3D"list-style-type: square;">
<li><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Go to cmd and enter services.ms=
c and right click on "Distributed Transaction Coordinator" and set startup =
type to Automatic (Delayed Start) and press start</span></li>
<li><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Go to Control panel -&gt; Admin=
istrative Tools -&gt;Component Services -&gt; Component Services -&gt; Open=
 Computers -&gt; My Computer -&gt; Distributed Transaction Coordinator -&gt=
; Right click on Local DTC -&gt;Select properties</span></li>
<li><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Select Security tab</span></li>
<li><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Click on Allow Remote Clients a=
nd Allow inbound and Allow Outbound</span></li>
<li><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Select No Authentication Requir=
ed</span></li>
<li><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">Apply</span></li>
</ul>
<p><br><strong><span style=3D"color: rgb(64,64,64);">DACPACS: &lt;&lt;&lt;&=
lt; Not needed anymore<br></span></strong><span style=3D"line-height: 1.428=
5715;">1) You need to run the dacpacs to update your local databases to the=
 latest schema. To do that, navigate to&nbsp;C:\Projects\Database\.build\<b=
r></span><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">2) Open a command prompt a=
t that location as Administrator and run app.all.full. Watch out for red er=
rors.<br></span><span style=3D"line-height: 1.4285715;">3) Run tests.all.fu=
ll</span></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong>SKYPE:</strong><br>1) If you are installing Skype, add this to y=
our hosts file to remove the annoying ads: 127.0.0.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp=
; <a href=3D"http://apps.skype.com" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow=
">apps.skype.com</a> # Skype Ads Blocker<br><br><strong>ZOOM:</strong><br>1=
) Management prefers to use Zoom for company-wide meetings. Download and in=
stall. You will be provided with a meeting room link if you are required to=
 join a Zoom meeting. You can then sign in using SSO.<br><br></p>
<p><strong>DYNAMIX STANDARD TIME</strong></p>
<p>You might get the exception "The time zone ID 'DynaMiX Standard Time' wa=
s not found on the local computer." To resolve this you should run "DynaMiX=
 Standard Time v11.reg". At time of writing, this can be found here:&nbsp;<=
/p>
<p>\\DSSTBSOFTWARE\Software\Dev Tools</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
